{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 36,
  "title": "The telephone",
  "description": "Name the parts of a phone, and talk about a call.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Everyone carries one of these, so the words are worth knowing. The names are a mixture of masculine and feminine, and the call itself is a noun you can make.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El teléfono, el móvil, el botón, el altavoz y el cargador are masculine. La llamada, la pantalla, la red y la batería are feminine. El botón is the button you press, and la pantalla is the screen you look at.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el móvil",
            "en": "the mobile phone"
          },
          {
            "es": "la pantalla",
            "en": "the screen"
          },
          {
            "es": "el botón",
            "en": "the button"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Talking about a call",
        "body": "Hacer una llamada is to make a call, and la llamada is the call itself. The words for the state of the phone are ordinary sentences: la batería está baja, the battery is low, el teléfono está en la mesa, the phone is on the table.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "la batería está baja",
            "en": "the battery is low"
          },
          {
            "es": "el teléfono está en la mesa",
            "en": "the phone is on the table"
          },
          {
            "es": "hago una llamada a mi madre",
            "en": "I make a call to my mother"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
